 ],
 "notes": "CardDemo's report request (transaction CR00, program CORPT00C): a monthly (the clock's month), yearly or custom date range is validated -- the custom dates through CALL 'CSUTLDTC' (CEEDAYS; the COBOL side links CardDemo's CSUTLDTC and tests/equivalence/le/ceedays.c, the Java side its proven port from carddemo-dateutil) -- and, once confirmed, the program submits its in-line JCL with the dates filled in, one WRITEQ TD to the JOBS queue per line, each line compared. A month above 12 is flagged by the program but still passed to CSUTLDTC, where the CEEDAYS model refuses it (IBM leaves open which condition a month outside 1-12 raises), so no scenario uses one -- nor a non-numeric month, which NUMVAL-C turns into 00. Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own."
